(* fs-records-b2s C2, security result, (K_s, K_r, T_max) = (2, 3, 2):
   injective record agreement at the Server.  Every acceptance of sequence t
   with plaintext m by a Server object, from the peer it installed for the
   identity ed_public(k), is matched by its own, distinct allocation of
   sequence t for m by a Beacon with that identity, pinning that Server key,
   in the same session (same key ID and root), unless the attacker holds k.
   Run twice: with fresh record plaintexts in the receive form in which
   failed opens are interleaved, and with adversary-chosen plaintexts in the
   fail-stop receive form (E21). *)
query s: bitstring, k: bitstring, kid: key_id, root: bitstring, t: nat, m: bitstring;
  inj-event(FsReceived(beacon_to_server(), s, ed_public(k), kid, root, t, m))
  ==> inj-event(FsSent(beacon_to_server(), s, ed_public(k), kid, root, t, m)) || attacker(k).

process FsRecordsB2sMain()
